IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`

-- P9-art-95-96: Chapter X "Codes of conduct and guidelines": Article 95 "Codes of conduct for voluntary application of
-- specific requirements" and Article 96 "Guidelines from the Commission on the implementation of this Regulation".
-- The Omnibus replaced Article 95(4) (small mid-cap enterprises added), Article 96(1) point (a) (Article 26 added) and
-- the second subparagraph of Article 96(1) (the Board involved, small mid-cap enterprises added), and inserted point (g).
-- Each replaced text is encoded as two functions, one for each version, quoted from the text it came from (the as-enacted
-- quotes are `src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:N`), and a dispatcher that gates on Article 113 and dispatches on the version in force.
-- Group General (2 August 2026) is after the Omnibus (27 July 2026), so the as-enacted branch of a dispatcher is dead for
-- every date on which the group applies: the as-enacted text is tested through its own function, and the dispatcher is
-- tested with a date on each side of 27 July 2026 (it answers NOTHING on both, because the group does not apply yet).
-- The AI Office, the Member States and the Commission are officials: no seat. What Article 95(4) and Article 96(1) mean to
-- a provider that is an SME or an SMC is asked in the provider seat.
-- The duties of this Chapter have no time limit and no stated consequence, except the publication date in Article 96(1)(g):
-- a late action reads FULFILLED, and they are listed in NOTES.md under "Rules with no breach path".

§ `Article 95: codes of conduct`

DECLARE `Art 95 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 95 the AI Office or a Member State`

DECLARE `Art 95 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 95(1) encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct intended to foster the voluntary application of the requirements of Chapter III Section 2`
    `Art 95(2) facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct concerning the voluntary application of specific requirements to all AI systems`
    `Art 95(4) take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise when encouraging and facilitating the drawing up of codes of conduct`

-- src:1421 | 1. The AI Office and the Member States shall encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct, including related governance mechanisms, intended to foster the voluntary application to AI systems, other than high-risk AI systems, of some or all of the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 taking into account the available technical solutions and industry best practices allowing for the application of such requirements.
@ref Art 95(1) (src:1421)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the codes of conduct are intended to foster the voluntary application to AI systems, other than high-risk AI systems, of some or all of the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 95(1) the AI Office and the Member States must encourage and facilitate the drawing up of the codes of conduct` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `the codes of conduct are intended to foster the voluntary application to AI systems, other than high-risk AI systems, of some or all of the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is about codes "intended to foster the voluntary application to AI systems, other than high-risk AI systems, of some or all of the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2"; other codes are not covered (a scope limit with no "only": ruling (c) of 2026-11-05)

@ref Art 95(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the codes of conduct are intended to foster the voluntary application to AI systems, other than high-risk AI systems, of some or all of the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 95 party` `Art 95 act`
`Art 95(1) the duty of the AI Office and the Member States to encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 95(1) the AI Office and the Member States must encourage and facilitate the drawing up of the codes of conduct` `the date asked` `the codes of conduct are intended to foster the voluntary application to AI systems, other than high-risk AI systems, of some or all of the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 95 the AI Office or a Member State`
        MUST `Art 95(1) encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct intended to foster the voluntary application of the requirements of Chapter III Section 2`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- src:1422 | 2. The AI Office and the Member States shall facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct concerning the voluntary application, including by deployers, of specific requirements to all AI systems, on the basis of clear objectives and key performance indicators to measure the achievement of those objectives, including elements such as, but not limited to:
-- src:1423 | (a) applicable elements provided for in Union ethical guidelines for trustworthy AI;
-- src:1424 | (b) assessing and minimising the impact of AI systems on environmental sustainability, including as regards energy-efficient programming and techniques for the efficient design, training and use of AI;
-- src:1425 | (c) promoting AI literacy, in particular that of persons dealing with the development, operation and use of AI;
-- src:1426 | (d) facilitating an inclusive and diverse design of AI systems, including through the establishment of inclusive and diverse development teams and the promotion of stakeholders’ participation in that process;
-- src:1427 | (e) assessing and preventing the negative impact of AI systems on vulnerable persons or groups of vulnerable persons, including as regards accessibility for persons with a disability, as well as on gender equality.
@ref Art 95(2) (src:1422-1427)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the codes of conduct concern the voluntary application, including by deployers, of specific requirements to all AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 95(2) the AI Office and the Member States must facilitate the drawing up of the codes of conduct` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `the codes of conduct concern the voluntary application, including by deployers, of specific requirements to all AI systems`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is about codes "concerning the voluntary application ... of specific requirements to all AI systems"; other codes are not covered (a scope limit with no "only": ruling (c) of 2026-11-05)

@ref Art 95(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the codes of conduct concern the voluntary application, including by deployers, of specific requirements to all AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 95 party` `Art 95 act`
`Art 95(2) the duty of the AI Office and the Member States to facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 95(2) the AI Office and the Member States must facilitate the drawing up of the codes of conduct` `the date asked` `the codes of conduct concern the voluntary application, including by deployers, of specific requirements to all AI systems`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 95 the AI Office or a Member State`
        MUST `Art 95(2) facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct concerning the voluntary application of specific requirements to all AI systems`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- "including elements such as, but not limited to": five elements, and the list is not closed.
DECLARE `Art 95(2) element` IS ONE OF
    `Art 95(2)(a) applicable elements provided for in Union ethical guidelines for trustworthy AI`
    `Art 95(2)(b) assessing and minimising the impact of AI systems on environmental sustainability`
    `Art 95(2)(c) promoting AI literacy`
    `Art 95(2)(d) facilitating an inclusive and diverse design of AI systems`
    `Art 95(2)(e) assessing and preventing the negative impact of AI systems on vulnerable persons or groups of vulnerable persons`
    `Art 95(2) another element`

@ref Art 95(2)
GIVEN `the element` IS AN `Art 95(2) element`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 95(2) the element is one the codes of conduct include` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the element`
    WHEN `Art 95(2)(a) applicable elements provided for in Union ethical guidelines for trustworthy AI` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Art 95(2)(b) assessing and minimising the impact of AI systems on environmental sustainability` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Art 95(2)(c) promoting AI literacy` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Art 95(2)(d) facilitating an inclusive and diverse design of AI systems` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Art 95(2)(e) assessing and preventing the negative impact of AI systems on vulnerable persons or groups of vulnerable persons` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Art 95(2) another element` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "including elements such as, but not limited to"

-- src:1428 | 3. Codes of conduct may be drawn up by individual providers or deployers of AI systems or by organisations representing them or by both, including with the involvement of any interested stakeholders and their representative organisations, including civil society organisations and academia. Codes of conduct may cover one or more AI systems taking into account the similarity of the intended purpose of the relevant systems.
@ref Art 95(3) (src:1428)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the person is an individual provider or deployer of AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an organisation representing providers or deployers of AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 95(3) the person may draw up codes of conduct` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such permission
    ELSE IF       `the person is an individual provider or deployer of AI systems`
               OR `the person is an organisation representing providers or deployers of AI systems`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- "or by both", and "including with the involvement of any interested stakeholders": neither is a condition
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to "individual providers or deployers of AI systems or ... organisations representing them or ... both"; for another person it is silent

@ref Art 95(3)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the number of AI systems the code of conduct covers` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 95(3) a code of conduct may cover the AI systems` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such permission
    ELSE IF `the number of AI systems the code of conduct covers` AT LEAST 1
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- "one or more AI systems, taking into account the similarity of the intended purpose": the similarity is a consideration, not a condition
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to cover "one or more AI systems"; a code that covers none is not covered

-- Article 95(4), as enacted: SMEs, including start-ups.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1972 | 4. The AI Office and the Member States shall take into account the specific interests and needs of SMEs, including start-ups, when encouraging and facilitating the drawing up of codes of conduct.
@ref Art 95(4) as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1972)
GIVEN `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 95(4) as enacted the specific interests and needs of the enterprise must be taken into account` MEANS
    IF `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): VERSION as enacted. The duty is to take into account "the specific interests and needs of SMEs, including start-ups"; for another enterprise it is silent

-- Article 95(4), as amended (Omnibus): SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs.
-- src:1430 | 4. The AI Office and the Member States shall take into account the specific interests and needs of SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs, when encouraging and facilitating the drawing up of codes of conduct.
@ref Art 95(4) as amended (src:1430)
GIVEN `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enterprise is an SMC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 95(4) as amended the specific interests and needs of the enterprise must be taken into account` MEANS
    IF `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` OR `the enterprise is an SMC`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): VERSION as amended. The duty is to take into account "the specific interests and needs of SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs"; for another enterprise it is silent

@ref Art 95(4)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enterprise is an SMC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 95(4) the AI Office and the Member States must take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 95(4) as enacted the specific interests and needs of the enterprise must be taken into account` `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up`  -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 95(4) as amended the specific interests and needs of the enterprise must be taken into account` `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` `the enterprise is an SMC`  -- VERSION as amended

@ref Art 95(4)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enterprise is an SMC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 95 party` `Art 95 act`
`Art 95(4) the duty of the AI Office and the Member States to take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 95(4) the AI Office and the Member States must take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise` `the date asked` `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` `the enterprise is an SMC`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 95 the AI Office or a Member State`
        MUST `Art 95(4) take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise when encouraging and facilitating the drawing up of codes of conduct`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 96: guidelines from the Commission`

DECLARE `Art 96 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 96 the Commission`

DECLARE `Art 96 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 96(1) develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation on the topic`
    `Art 96(1) involve the Board when issuing the guidelines`
    `Art 96(1) pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary when issuing the guidelines`
    `Art 96(1)(g) publish the guidelines on the complementarity and proportionality of the requirements`
    `Art 96(2) update the guidelines previously adopted`

-- "in particular on": (a) to (f) as enacted; (g) and Article 26 in point (a) as amended.
DECLARE `Art 96(1) topic` IS ONE OF
    `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the requirements and obligations referred to in Articles 8 to 15`
    `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the obligations referred to in Article 25`
    `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the obligations referred to in Article 26`
    `Art 96(1)(b) the prohibited practices referred to in Article 5`
    `Art 96(1)(c) the practical implementation of the provisions related to substantial modification`
    `Art 96(1)(d) the practical implementation of transparency obligations laid down in Article 50`
    `Art 96(1)(e) detailed information on the relationship of this Regulation with the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I, as well as with other relevant Union law`
    `Art 96(1)(f) the application of the definition of an AI system as set out in Article 3, point (1)`
    `Art 96(1)(g) the practical implementation of Article 8(2), Article 9(10) and Article 17(3)`
    `Art 96(1) another topic`

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1975 | 1. The Commission shall develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation, and in particular on:
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1976 | (a)
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1977 | the application of the requirements and obligations referred to in Articles 8 to 15 and in Article 25;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1978 | (b)
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1979 | the prohibited practices referred to in Article 5;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1980 | (c)
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1981 | the practical implementation of the provisions related to substantial modification;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1982 | (d)
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1983 | the practical implementation of transparency obligations laid down in Article 50;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1984 | (e)
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1985 | detailed information on the relationship of this Regulation with the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I, as well as with other relevant Union law, including as regards consistency in their enforcement;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1986 | (f)
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1987 | the application of the definition of an AI system as set out in Article 3, point (1).
@ref Art 96(1) as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1975-1987)
GIVEN `the topic` IS AN `Art 96(1) topic`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the topic`
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the requirements and obligations referred to in Articles 8 to 15` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as enacted
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the obligations referred to in Article 25` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as enacted
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the obligations referred to in Article 26` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): point (a) names Article 25 and not Article 26 as enacted
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(b) the prohibited practices referred to in Article 5` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as enacted
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(c) the practical implementation of the provisions related to substantial modification` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as enacted
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(d) the practical implementation of transparency obligations laid down in Article 50` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as enacted
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(e) detailed information on the relationship of this Regulation with the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I, as well as with other relevant Union law` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as enacted
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(f) the application of the definition of an AI system as set out in Article 3, point (1)` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as enacted
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(g) the practical implementation of Article 8(2), Article 9(10) and Article 17(3)` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): point (g) is not in the text as enacted
    WHEN `Art 96(1) another topic` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "and in particular on" names points (a) to (f) and does not say "only"

-- src:1434 | 1. The Commission shall develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation, and in particular on:
-- src:1436 | (a) the application of the requirements and obligations referred to in Articles 8 to 15 and in Articles 25 and 26;
-- src:1438 | (b) the prohibited practices referred to in Article 5;
-- src:1439 | (c) the practical implementation of the provisions related to substantial modification;
-- src:1440 | (d) the practical implementation of transparency obligations laid down in Article 50;
-- src:1441 | (e) detailed information on the relationship of this Regulation with the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I, as well as with other relevant Union law, including as regards consistency in their enforcement;
-- src:1442 | (f) the application of the definition of an AI system as set out in Article 3, point (1);
-- src:1444 | (g) the practical implementation of Article 8(2), Article 9(10) and Article 17(3) in accordance with the principle of complementarity and proportionality, with a view to ensuring consistency, avoiding duplication and minimising additional burdens when complying with the requirements of this Regulation and the requirements of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I; such guidelines shall be published by 1 August 2027.
@ref Art 96(1) as amended (src:1434-1444)
GIVEN `the topic` IS AN `Art 96(1) topic`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the topic`
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the requirements and obligations referred to in Articles 8 to 15` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the obligations referred to in Article 25` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the obligations referred to in Article 26` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(b) the prohibited practices referred to in Article 5` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(c) the practical implementation of the provisions related to substantial modification` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(d) the practical implementation of transparency obligations laid down in Article 50` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(e) detailed information on the relationship of this Regulation with the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I, as well as with other relevant Union law` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(f) the application of the definition of an AI system as set out in Article 3, point (1)` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Art 96(1)(g) the practical implementation of Article 8(2), Article 9(10) and Article 17(3)` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Art 96(1) another topic` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "and in particular on" names points (a) to (g) and does not say "only"

@ref Art 96(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the topic` IS AN `Art 96(1) topic`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 96(1) the Commission must develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation on the topic` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `the topic`  -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `the topic`  -- VERSION as amended

@ref Art 96(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the topic` IS AN `Art 96(1) topic`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 96 party` `Art 96 act`
`Art 96(1) the duty of the Commission to develop guidelines on the topic` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 96(1) the Commission must develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation on the topic` `the date asked` `the topic`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 96 the Commission`
        MUST `Art 96(1) develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation on the topic`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- Point (g) says the guidelines "shall be published by 1 August 2027": a date in the text, so the rule has a breach path.
-- The caller states the day from which the time is counted (the day the duty began: not before the date asked).
@ref Art 96(1)(g)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the day from which the time is counted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 96 party` `Art 96 act`
`Art 96(1)(g) the duty of the Commission to publish the guidelines by 1 August 2027` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Article 113 gives this provision its date of application
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN FULFILLED  -- VERSION as enacted. Point (g) is not in the text as enacted, so nothing is owed
         WHEN `as amended` THEN                                      -- VERSION as amended
             PARTY `Art 96 the Commission`
             MUST `Art 96(1)(g) publish the guidelines on the complementarity and proportionality of the requirements`
             WITHIN (Day (Date 1 8 2027)) MINUS (Day `the day from which the time is counted`)
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST BREACH BY `Art 96 the Commission` BECAUSE "the guidelines on the practical implementation of Article 8(2), Article 9(10) and Article 17(3) were not published by 1 August 2027"

