    `Art 96(1) SMEs, including start-ups`
    `Art 96(1) SMCs`
    `Art 96(1) local public authorities`
    `Art 96(1) the sectors most likely to be affected by this Regulation`
    `Art 96(1) another beneficiary`

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1988 | When issuing such guidelines, the Commission shall pay particular attention to the needs of SMEs including start-ups, of local public authorities and of the sectors most likely to be affected by this Regulation.
@ref Art 96(1) second subparagraph, as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1988)
GIVEN `the beneficiary` IS AN `Art 96(1) beneficiary`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the beneficiary`
    WHEN `Art 96(1) SMEs, including start-ups` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as enacted
    WHEN `Art 96(1) SMCs` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): the second subparagraph as enacted names SMEs including start-ups, local public authorities and the sectors most likely to be affected, and not SMCs
    WHEN `Art 96(1) local public authorities` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as enacted
    WHEN `Art 96(1) the sectors most likely to be affected by this Regulation` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as enacted
    WHEN `Art 96(1) another beneficiary` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence names three beneficiaries and does not say "only"

-- src:1446 | When issuing such guidelines, the Commission shall involve the Board and pay particular attention to the needs of SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs, of local public authorities and of the sectors most likely to be affected by this Regulation.
@ref Art 96(1) second subparagraph, as amended (src:1446)
GIVEN `the beneficiary` IS AN `Art 96(1) beneficiary`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the beneficiary`
    WHEN `Art 96(1) SMEs, including start-ups` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Art 96(1) SMCs` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Art 96(1) local public authorities` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Art 96(1) the sectors most likely to be affected by this Regulation` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Art 96(1) another beneficiary` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence names four beneficiaries and does not say "only"

@ref Art 96(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the beneficiary` IS AN `Art 96(1) beneficiary`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 96(1) the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary when issuing the guidelines` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` `the beneficiary`  -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` `the beneficiary`  -- VERSION as amended

@ref Art 96(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the beneficiary` IS AN `Art 96(1) beneficiary`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 96 party` `Art 96 act`
`Art 96(1) the duty of the Commission to pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 96(1) the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary when issuing the guidelines` `the date asked` `the beneficiary`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 96 the Commission`
        MUST `Art 96(1) pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary when issuing the guidelines`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- The third subparagraph: unchanged by the Omnibus.
-- src:1448 | The guidelines referred to in the first subparagraph of this paragraph shall take due account of the generally acknowledged state of the art on AI, as well as of relevant harmonised standards and common specifications that are referred to in Articles 40 and 41, or of those harmonised standards or technical specifications that are set out pursuant to Union harmonisation law.
@ref Art 96(1) third subparagraph (src:1448)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the guidelines take due account of the generally acknowledged state of the art on AI` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidelines take due account of the relevant harmonised standards and common specifications referred to in Articles 40 and 41, or of those harmonised standards or technical specifications that are set out pursuant to Union harmonisation law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 96(1) the guidelines take due account of the state of the art and the standards` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is required
    ELSE IF       `the guidelines take due account of the generally acknowledged state of the art on AI`
              AND `the guidelines take due account of the relevant harmonised standards and common specifications referred to in Articles 40 and 41, or of those harmonised standards or technical specifications that are set out pursuant to Union harmonisation law`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The guidelines ... shall take due account of the generally acknowledged state of the art on AI, as well as of relevant harmonised standards and common specifications" (a requirement of manner: not met means the requirement is not met)

-- src:1449 | 2. At the request of the Member States or the AI Office, or on its own initiative, the Commission shall update guidelines previously adopted when deemed necessary.
@ref Art 96(2) (src:1449)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `guidelines have previously been adopted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission deems the update necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 96(2) the Commission must update the guidelines previously adopted` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF NOT `guidelines have previously been adopted`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to update "guidelines previously adopted"
         ELSE IF `the Commission deems the update necessary`
              THEN JUST TRUE  -- "at the request of the Member States or the AI Office, or on its own initiative": a request is not a condition
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Commission shall update guidelines previously adopted when deemed necessary" (a "when" gate on a duty that is not met: fork F-96-2)

@ref Art 96(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `guidelines have previously been adopted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission deems the update necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 96 party` `Art 96 act`
`Art 96(2) the duty of the Commission to update the guidelines previously adopted` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 96(2) the Commission must update the guidelines previously adopted` `the date asked` `guidelines have previously been adopted` `the Commission deems the update necessary`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 96 the Commission`
        MUST `Art 96(2) update the guidelines previously adopted`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts
